WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.283
When the hot-air balloon was ready, Oz sent word to the people of the Emerald City.

2
00:00:05.284 --> 00:00:10.448
Everyone gathered to see Oz and Dorothy depart.

3
00:00:10.449 --> 00:00:16.320
Oz climbed into the basket and shouted to the crowd, "I am off to see a brother wizard!

4
00:00:16.321 --> 00:00:20.314
While I am gone, the Scarecrow will be your ruler.

5
00:00:20.315 --> 00:00:30.310
Obey him as you would obey me."

6
00:00:30.311 --> 00:00:33.463
Soon the balloon was tugging at the ropes.

7
00:00:33.464 --> 00:00:38.417
"Come, Dorothy," shouted the Wizard. "Before the balloon flies away."

8
00:00:38.418 --> 00:00:42.949
"Wait. I can't find Toto," answered Dorothy.

9
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:49.121
She spotted Toto and picked him up. "You're a very naughty dog," she said.

10
00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:56.090
Oz reached out his hands to help Dorothy into the balloon when suddenly a gust of wind snapped the ropes.

11
00:00:56.091 --> 00:01:00.071
The balloon quickly rose into the air without her.

12
00:01:00.072 --> 00:01:03.080
"Come back!" she screamed.

13
00:01:03.081 --> 00:01:10.299
"I can't, my dear," called Oz from the basket. "Good-bye."

14
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:15.761
The balloon rose higher and higher in the sky until it vanished behind the clouds.

15
00:01:15.762 --> 00:01:20.405
That was the last anyone saw of the Wonderful Wizard of Oz.

16
00:01:20.406 --> 00:01:24.285
Dorothy dropped to the ground and cried.

17
00:01:24.286 --> 00:01:31.191
"I'll never go home. Never," she moaned.

18
00:01:31.192 --> 00:01:35.712
The next day Dorothy and her friends gathered in the throne room.

19
00:01:35.713 --> 00:01:41.389
The Scarecrow was sitting on the throne, and the others stood respectfully in front of him.

20
00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.175
"We are not unlucky," said the Scarecrow.

21
00:01:44.176 --> 00:01:48.013
"For this palace and the Emerald City belong to us.

22
00:01:48.014 --> 00:01:52.776
Now if only we could convince Dorothy to live here with us."

23
00:01:52.777 --> 00:01:56.074
"But I don't want to live here," cried Dorothy.

24
00:01:56.075 --> 00:02:01.326
"I want to go home. I want to see Aunt Em and Uncle Henry."

25
00:02:01.327 --> 00:02:05.300
"What can we do?" asked the Tin Man.

26
00:02:05.301 --> 00:02:12.156
The Scarecrow gave it careful thought and said, "Call the Winged Monkeys and ask them to carry you over the desert."

27
00:02:12.157 --> 00:02:19.395
"I never thought of that," shouted Dorothy joyfully, and she ran to get the golden hat.

28
00:02:19.396 --> 00:02:23.348
When Dorothy returned, wearing the hat, she spread her arms.

29
00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:27.643
And she said the magic words, "By my command."

30
00:02:27.644 --> 00:02:31.912
Soon the Monkey King arrived and said, "What do you command?"

31
00:02:31.913 --> 00:02:36.851
"I want you to fly me back to Kansas," said Dorothy.

32
00:02:36.852 --> 00:02:42.338
"We cannot," said the King. "Our ability to fly is limited to Oz.

33
00:02:42.339 --> 00:02:48.028
Another command we will gladly obey, but we cannot fly across the Great Desert."

34
00:02:48.029 --> 00:02:53.520
The King bowed and flew away. Dorothy was ready to cry again.

35
00:02:53.521 --> 00:02:57.725
"Don't cry," said the kindhearted Tin Man.

36
00:02:57.726 --> 00:03:03.817
"No, don't cry," said the Scarecrow. "Let us ask the soldier for advice."

37
00:03:03.818 --> 00:03:11.573
They asked the soldier and he said, "Glinda's castle is on the edge of the desert. She might know a way across."

38
00:03:11.574 --> 00:03:15.054
"Who is Glinda?" asked the Scarecrow.

39
00:03:15.055 --> 00:03:20.383
"She is the Good Witch of the South," replied the soldier.

40
00:03:20.384 --> 00:03:24.551
"How can we get to her castle?" asked Dorothy hopefully.

41
00:03:24.552 --> 00:03:28.218
"It is both easy and hard," answered the soldier.

42
00:03:28.219 --> 00:03:32.065
"The road is straight south, but there are many dangers."

43
00:03:32.066 --> 00:03:36.489
Dorothy and her friends thanked the soldier for his advice.

44
00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:39.780
"The answer is simple," said the Scarecrow.

45
00:03:39.781 --> 00:03:43.358
"Yes, it is," said the Lion.

46
00:03:43.359 --> 00:03:46.608
"We'll leave tomorrow," said the Tin Man.

47
00:03:46.609 --> 00:03:50.062
"I think that's best," said the Scarecrow.

48
00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:53.874
"Are you all coming with me?" asked Dorothy, surprised.

49
00:03:53.875 --> 00:04:01.190
"Of course," said the Lion. "None of us would have met Oz if it weren't for you."

50
00:04:01.191 --> 00:04:04.856
Early the next morning, the friends gathered at the city gate.

51
00:04:04.857 --> 00:04:14.005
The gatekeeper removed their glasses and said to the Scarecrow, "You must return to us as soon as you can because you are our ruler now."

52
00:04:14.006 --> 00:04:20.248
"I will," said the Scarecrow. "But first I must help Dorothy get home."

53
00:04:20.249 --> 00:04:23.213
Dorothy was glad to be on her way home.

54
00:04:23.214 --> 00:04:28.509
The others were happy too, and they talked about how great the wizard of Oz had been.

55
00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:31.567
Dorothy knew that Oz wasn't a great wizard.

56
00:04:31.568 --> 00:04:40.223
He hadn't returned her to Kansas, but he had tried so she forgave him.

